            "text": "Press Play below to start the backing track, and follow the tab. A triad is a chord played as three notes, here on the G, B and high e strings. One small shape is G. The same shape slid up the neck is C, slid further up it is D, and then it comes back down to G.\nStrike the three strings together on every beat, four times for each chord.\nKeep going until the slide to the next chord lands on beat 1."
